From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: add MLO BH per-link channel-switch event handling

Add dedicated handlers for CTRL-EVENT-STARTED-LINK-CHANNEL-SWITCH and
CTRL-EVENT-LINK-CHANNEL-SWITCH wpa_supplicant events. These events carry
a link_id field identifying which MLO link the channel switch applies to,
allowing the per-link chanspec to be forwarded to the correct neighbor
endpoint's wpaCtrl interface.

Previously both CTRL-EVENT-STARTED-LINK-CHANNEL-SWITCH and
CTRL-EVENT-LINK-CHANNEL-SWITCH were dispatched to the same generic
s_chanSwitchStartedEvtCb / s_chanSwitchEvtCb handlers which have no
awareness of MLO link IDs. Channel updates for non-primary BH links were
therefore routed to the wrong radio.

Also make s_chanSwitchCb use ifName (was _UNUSED) so the EP lookup can
identify the backhaul endpoint, and resume the bkh chanspec refresh
timer on CSA completion.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
